Height field apron

Adds b3HeightFieldDef::apronSides, a mask of the grid sides that touch another
height field. The height and material arrays of the definition are then padded
by one sample on every side, and the edge flags along a marked side are
computed against the padding, which holds the neighbour's samples. Two height
fields placed side by side flag their shared border as flat when the surface
is continuous, so capsules and hulls skip the ghost contact on it.

A sphere has no such filter across shapes, so its edge or vertex contact on a
flat border edge is replaced by the contact against the plane of the
triangle, the same contact the neighbouring height field makes with its face.

The apron is read while the height field is created and is not stored. The
blob, its bounds and its hash are the same as without an apron, and a zero
apronSides is the unmodified behaviour.

b3DumpHeightData writes the interior grid only, so b3LoadHeightField returns
a height field without an apron.

